          {
            "scoreKey": "task_orientation",
            "headline": "Task Orientation: reflecting on this class",
            "source": {
              "type": "score_only"
            },
            "summary": "This describes how often class goals and learning tasks feel clear and you stay involved in the work. A higher mean means you reported these experiences more often; it does not establish your ability, effort or responsibility. The displayed value is the mean of eight complete responses on a 1–5 frequency scale. There are no high/low categories or comparison norms.",
            "bands": [],
            "guidance": [
              {
                "category": "reflection",
                "text": "Which part of a current task is clear, and which part needs explanation?"
              },
              {
                "category": "environment",
                "text": "Try asking for the next step or a clearer goal. A teacher or trusted adult can help adjust an unclear task."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "limitations": [
          "Your answers describe your perspective in this particular class. They cannot establish a teacher’s quality, classmates’ intentions or the causes of an experience.",
          "These original English items are separated from the 56-item WIHIC. Standalone eight-item administration and this digital feedback have not been validated. This is not a validated Chinese questionnaire.",
          "A score is shown only when all eight answers are present. Missing answers are not scored as zero or filled in. No local norms, thresholds or rankings are supplied.",
          "An uncomfortable or unfair experience is not your fault. This questionnaire does not ask you to challenge a teacher or fix the classroom on your own; a trusted adult can help you decide what feels safe."
        ],
        "disclaimer": "For research and supportive reflection on classroom experiences. Do not use for teacher appraisal, school ranking, diagnosis or student selection. Discuss concerns with a trusted adult regardless of the score. There is no combined WIHIC total.",
